Parity notes (web -> native):
  - Recharts AreaChart -> code-built Canvas renderer: a speed Area on the left axis (token
    TsChartSpeedBrush = web CHART_COLORS[0] cyan) + a power Area on the right axis in kW (token
    TsChartPowerBrush = web CHART_COLORS[1] violet), each pre-normalized to its own ratio so it occupies
    the full vertical range exactly as the web's two YAxis do (speed anchored at 0; power across
    min..max so regen stays visible), fillOpacity 0.2.
  - Persistent playhead <ReferenceLine x={cursorTime} stroke="#00b4d8" strokeWidth={2}
    strokeDasharray="4 2" /> -> a dashed TsColorInfoBrush line at the current replay index, repositioned
    without rebuilding the area geometry.
  - Interaction: web useSyncedCursor (onMouseMove writes activeLabel) + the chart onClick + the
    ChartCursorBridge (useSyncedReferenceLineX -> onSeekToIndex) are reproduced through the shared
    ChartCursorSyncGroup (P1/S8): pointer move / tap / Left|Right|Home|End keys broadcast the hovered
    sample's `time`; the view-model bridges that group to nearestIndexByTime -> advances CurrentIndex
    (the playhead) and raises SeekToIndexRequested (web onSeekToIndex). A host drives the playhead back
    via SeekTo(int) (web currentIndex). lastForwardedRef de-bounce preserved (one forward per index).
  - timelineData projection: X = minutes since the first sample (web (ts - t0)/60_000, toFixed(3));
    speed convertSpeedFromSI to the user's unit; power kept verbatim in kW (web `power ?? 0`).
  - Empty gate data.length > 0 (web); ALL 6 states rendered (loading / loaded / empty / error / stale /
    offline) since the native feature-view owns its cache-then-network drive-telemetry read.
  - i18n (ILocalizer): every web key reproduced — replay.timeline.title ("Speed & Power Timeline"),
    .subtitle ("Click to seek replay position"), .aria ("Trip replay speed and power timeline area
    chart"), .speed ("Speed"), .power ("Power"), .noData ("No telemetry data available") + .summary and
    the self-fetch chrome (.errorTitle/.refresh/.error*, common.loading/retry/stale/offline). No English
    literals in native code.
  - Data bound through the shared P1/S8 state-holder (ITripReplayChartsSource cache-then-network over
    get_api_v1_drives + get_api_v1_drives_driveID_telemetry); the view performs no HTTP. Diagnostics emit
    "view.opened slug=TripReplayCharts" (P1/S11).
  - Accessibility: chart is a focusable Image-role peer with a spoken AutomationName (sample count),
    arrow/Home/End keyboard seeking, Narrator names on the legend + freshness/refresh chrome; axis swatches
    marked AccessibilityView.Raw.

